<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds closed lower, in line with other markets, after strong U.S. data indicating rates may have to rise soon.</p>
<p>The Chicago purchasing managers index came in at 60.0 percent in August compared with 51.2 percent the previous month.</p>
<p>&quot;Markets agree that the (Federal Reserve) will have to raise rates, but the calendar isn't very clear,&quot; said a trader.</p>
<p>Domestic bonds remained pressured by the dollar's lacklustre performance against the mark, despite supportive comments from Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer.</p>
</text>
